also the very fact that cloudflare's "white lie" would
work is that they have access to their ZSK all the time...
which is a valid assumption with MY zones!  The Pi zero
holds the ZSKs and actually has to sign them; to have to
sign a fresh key dynamically instead of pulling one out
of the contiguous ranges delimited by either the names
themselves (NSEC) or hashes of those names (NSEC3), is
the WHOLE point of using NSEC -- it's to have a finite
set of pre-signed records to deny the existence of the
infinitely many possible names out there.  Cloudflare can
do this merely means that they don't have this model; but
not everyone is Cloudflare, both a global CDN and a DNS
server!  (In particular DNS isn't always, well... at
least trust-model wise, not everyone is a master and has
persistent access to the zone-signing keys.  (Actually
this is sort of making me regret doing that signing thing
on the Pi because that means the Pi has to be alive for
at least once a week.... yikes :x  Probably should have
just done it on the VPSes.))
